SetupCache: do not truncate the input-gamut compression cache key.

Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-08.
Three %.17g doubles and the algorithm need more than 64 bytes. Formatting
them into one fixed buffer could merge distinct compression settings into
one LUT entry. Append the algorithm and each complete double separately.
Numerical builders are unchanged; default settings retain the same key.

diff --git a/engine/src/core/setup_cache.cpp b/engine/src/core/setup_cache.cpp
--- a/engine/src/core/setup_cache.cpp
+++ b/engine/src/core/setup_cache.cpp
@@ -38,9 +38,12 @@ std::string tc_lut_key(const Profile& film, const SettingsParams& settings,
     key += buf;
     if (compress.active) {
-        std::snprintf(buf, sizeof buf, "|c%s,%.17g,%.17g,%.17g", compress.algorithm.c_str(),
-                      compress.knee[0], compress.knee[1], compress.knee[2]);
-        key += buf;
+        key += "|c";
+        key += compress.algorithm;
+        for (double knee : compress.knee) {
+            std::snprintf(buf, sizeof buf, ",%.17g", knee);
+            key += buf;
+        }
     } else {
         key += "|c0";
     }
     // The window and surface parameters come from the profile, and a profile
